## Endpoint: POST /api/owners — full request-handling path

The base path `/api` comes from `@RequestMapping("/api")` on the controller; the operation path `/owners` comes from the generated `OwnersApi` interface (`PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"`). Combined route: **POST /api/owners**.

---

### 1. Controller method

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class declaration (lines 60-63): `@RestController`, `@CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders = "errors, content-type")`, `@RequestMapping("/api")`, `implements OwnersApi`.

The handler is `addOwner` (lines 113-192), overriding the interface default. The HTTP mapping itself lives on the interface method (see section 4). Body of the method, in execution order:

```java
113  @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
114  @Override
115  public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
116      HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
117      Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
118      String address = normalizeAddress(owner.getAddress());
119      if (address.isEmpty()) { return ... BAD_REQUEST; }
122      owner.setAddress(address);
123      String telephone = toE164(owner.getTelephone());
124      if (telephone == null) { return ... BAD_REQUEST; }
127      owner.setTelephone(telephone);
128      if (owner.getEmail() != null) {
129          String email = normalizeEmail(owner.getEmail());
130          if (email == null) { return ... BAD_REQUEST; }
133          owner.setEmail(email);
      }
135      if (owner.getPostcode() != null && !isValidPostcode(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity())) {
136          return ... BAD_REQUEST; }
138      LocalDate effectiveRegistrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
139      if (effectiveRegistrationDate == null) effectiveRegistrationDate = LocalDate.now();
142      LocalDate registrationDate = toBusinessDay(effectiveRegistrationDate);
143      owner.setRegistrationDate(registrationDate);
144      if (countOwnersInCity(owner.getCity()) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY) return ... CONFLICT;
147      if (countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY) return ... TOO_MANY_REQUESTS;
      // household assignment ...
173      String identityKey = identityKey(...);
174      for (Owner existing : findAllOwners()) { if (identityKey matches) return ... CONFLICT; }
180      owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(owner.getCity(), owner.getLastName()));
181      owner.setMembershipNumber(membershipNumber(...));
182      owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
183      this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
184      OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
185      AUDIT.info("owner created: id={} ...", ...);
188      ownerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(isBulkSignupDay());
189      headers.setLocation(.../api/owners/{id}...);
191      return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
  }
```

**Ordered side effects / validations inside the controller (all AFTER bean validation):**

1. **Maps DTO → `Owner`** via `ownerMapper.toOwner` (line 117).
2. **Address normalization** (line 118, method lines 453-471): trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE. Empty result → **400**.
3. **Telephone → E.164** (line 123, `toE164` lines 561-581): strips spaces/dashes/brackets; `+`→keep, leading `0`→`+61` (AU), else `+1` (NANP); must be 8-15 digits and pass national-length check (`hasValidNationalLength`, lines 592-600: `+61` needs 9 national digits, `+1` needs 10). Invalid → **400**.
4. **Email normalization** (only if present; lines 128-134, `normalizeEmail` lines 645-651): trims, regex `^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$`, lower-cases. Invalid → **400**.
5. **Postcode validation** (only if present; lines 135-137, `isValidPostcode` lines 624-635): must be `[0-9]{4}` and within region range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099 via `OwnerLocality.forCity`). Invalid → **400**.
6. **Default + adjust `registrationDate`** (lines 138-143): null → `LocalDate.now()`; then `toBusinessDay` rolls Sat→Mon, Sun→Mon (lines 325-334).
7. **Per-city cap** (line 144): `countOwnersInCity >= 50` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) → **409 CONFLICT**.
8. **Per-day cap** (line 147): `countOwnersRegisteredOn >= 100` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) → **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.
9. **Household assignment** (lines 150-170): finds existing owners with same normalized lastName+address (`householdKey` lines 482-487), assigns a deterministic `householdId` (SHA-256, first 12 hex upper-cased, lines 501-514), and **saves each existing household member whose householdId changed** (`this.clinicService.saveOwner(member)` at line 167 — a side-effecting write to OTHER rows).
10. **Duplicate/identity check** (lines 171-179): builds `identityKey` = `telephone|email|householdId` (lines 529-533); if any existing owner matches → **409 CONFLICT**.
11. **Derived fields set on the new owner** before save: `customerCode` (line 180, `nextCustomerCode` lines 384-394, format `CITY3-LAST3-NNNN`), `membershipNumber` (line 181, `membershipNumber` lines 406-408, `<customerCode>-M<YY>`), `namesakeCount` (line 182, `countNamesakes` lines 419-428).
12. **Persist** via `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (line 183).
13. **Audit log side effect** (lines 185-187): writes one line to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (`LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT")`, line 66).
14. **Response mapping** (line 184) + `bulkSignupWarning` flag (line 188, `isBulkSignupDay` lines 369-371: true when >80 owners today) + `Location` header (lines 189-190) → **201 CREATED**.

Note: no email is sent and no Spring event is published anywhere in this path — the only "notification" is the AUDIT logger line.

---

### 2. Request DTO (`@RequestBody`) — Bean Validation annotations

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java` (OpenAPI-generated; validation annotations are on the getters)

| Field | Line | Bean Validation annotations |
|---|---|---|
| `firstName` | 73 | `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 30)` |
| `lastName` | 94 | `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 30)` |
| `address` | 115 | `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = ".*\\S.*")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 255)` |
| `city` | 136 | `@NotNull` `@Pattern(regexp = ".*\\S.*")` `@Size(min = 1, max = 80)` |
| `telephone` | 157 | `@NotNull` `@Size(min = 1, max = 20)` |
| `email` | 178 | `@Size(max = 255)` `@jakarta.validation.constraints.Email` |
| `postcode` | 199 | `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{4}$")` |
| `registrationDate` | 220 | `@Valid` (LocalDate) |
| `sharesHousehold` | 242 | none (write-only hint, never persisted) |

No custom validators. These fire before the controller body because the interface param is annotated `@Valid @RequestBody` (see section 4).

---

### 3. Service layer

**Interface:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` — `saveOwner` (line 59), `findAllOwners` (line 57), `findOwnerByLastName` (line 61).

**Impl:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`

```java
232  @Override
233  @Transactional
234  public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
235      ownerRepository.save(owner);
236  }
```
```java
125  @Override
126  @Transactional(readOnly = true)
127  public Collection<Owner> findAllOwners() throws DataAccessException {
128      return ownerRepository.findAll();
129  }
```

The service layer is a thin pass-through: `saveOwner` is `@Transactional` and simply delegates to `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. No validation, duplicate checks, defaults, timestamps, events, or emails at this layer — all business logic lives in the controller (section 1). Note the controller's `addOwner` is NOT itself `@Transactional`, so each `saveOwner` call (including the household-member updates) is its own transaction.

---

### 4. `@Valid`, HTTP mapping, exception handlers

**Interface / mapping + `@Valid`:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`
- Interface annotated `@Validated` (line 44).
- `addOwner` mapping (lines 79-87):
```java
@RequestMapping(method = RequestMethod.POST, value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,
    produces = { "application/json" }, consumes = { "application/json" })
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(...) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) { ... }
```
So the `@Valid @RequestBody` triggers Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`; a failure throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException` before the controller override runs.

**Exception handler:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` — `@ControllerAdvice` (line 49):
- `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException` (lines 134-170) → **400**, builds a `ProblemDetail` with `schemaValidationErrors` and `errors` field lists from the `BindingResult`.
- `handleAccessDeniedException` (lines 85-88) → re-throws so Security produces 403/entry-point (prevents it being masked as 500).
- `handleDataIntegrityViolationException` (lines 114-125) → **404**.
- `handleGeneralException` (lines 97-104) → **500** fallback.

No custom `ConstraintValidator` classes exist in the project.

---

### 5. Repository save + JPA entity lifecycle

**Owner entity:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`
- `@Entity`, `@Table(name = "owners")`, `extends Person` (lines 35-37).
- Entity-level Bean Validation constraints (enforced by Hibernate on flush, in addition to the DTO's): `address` `@NotEmpty` (39), `city` `@NotEmpty` (43), `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(regexp = "^(\\+[0-9]{8,15}|[0-9]{10})$", ...)` (47-49). `email`, `postcode`, `registrationDate`, `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount` have no constraints. `pets` is `@OneToMany(cascade = ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = EAGER)` (73-74) — cascade ALL means saving an owner cascades to its pets.
- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks**: there are NO `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@PreUpdate`, NO `@EntityListeners`, NO `@CreatedDate`/`@LastModifiedDate`/auditing anywhere on `Owner`, `Person`, or `BaseEntity`. `registrationDate` is set manually in the controller, not by an auditing callback.

**Base classes:**
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java` — `@MappedSuperclass`; `firstName` `@NotEmpty` (32), `lastName` `@NotEmpty` (36).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java` — `@MappedSuperclass`; `id` is `@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)` (33-34). `isNew()` returns `id == null`.

**Repository save (jpa profile):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` (`@Repository`, `@Profile("jpa")`):
```java
92  @Override
93  public void save(Owner owner) {
94      if (owner.getId() == null) {
95          this.em.persist(owner);
96      } else {
97          this.em.merge(owner);
98      }
99  }
```
`findAll()` (lines 102-107) runs `SELECT owner FROM Owner owner`. Note the controller calls `findAllOwners()` multiple times per create (city cap, day cap, household scan, duplicate scan, namesake count, customer-code sequence), each a full table scan.

There is also a Spring-Data variant `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` and a JDBC impl `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, selected by the active Spring profile (`jpa` / `spring-data-jpa` / `jdbc`); the JPA one above is the representative implementation.

---

### 6. Spring Security

**On the endpoint:** `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` on `addOwner` (OwnerRestControllerV1.java line 113). `@roles` resolves to the bean below; `OWNER_ADMIN` = `"ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"`.

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java` (line 8): `public final String OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN";`

**Security config is toggled by property `petclinic.security.enable`:**
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/DisableSecurityConfig.java` — `@ConditionalOnProperty(name = "petclinic.security.enable", havingValue = "false")`; disables CSRF and permits all requests. When active, the `@PreAuthorize` still applies only if method security is enabled.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java` — the enabled-security counterpart (HTTP Basic, JDBC users/roles via `select username,role from roles where username=?`).

All V1 owner endpoints require `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. (The V2 controller at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java` uses the same role but does not expose a create-owner POST; V1 is the one handling POST /api/owners.)

